# std/rgrep's image (design/caos-expr.md, Phase 3): build this directory as a
# Rust project with rustc. `--src:@=.` hands rustc this whole tree (its
# Cargo.toml + src/; rustc skips the caos metadata — .caos-expr, DEPS,
# DEEP-DEPS/); `--runner:@=DEEP-DEPS/runner` is the base its `finish` curries the
# built binary onto. Both deps are named by LOCAL deep-deps mounts (declared in
# DEPS) rather than /std, so std carries no ambient self-reference. The result is
# curry(runner, worker1=<the compiled binary>) — a ready-to-run worker in the
# shared runner pool.
run DEEP-DEPS/rustc -- --src:@=. --runner:@=DEEP-DEPS/runner
